      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "OLINDAH (6) showed talent as a juvenile, and resumed with a very impressive win fresh up for the season here 2 weeks ago, coming from near last to score by nearly a length as the favourite. She is to be ridden by 4kg claiming apprentice Robyn Lynch this time, and if she gets a clear run, she can take the next step immediately. MISS LYRA (5) continues to improve with racing this season, and was second by less than a length here 4 weeks ago. She drops a kilo in weight, and can go one better. PEAK A BOOM (8) ran a better race second up when finishing fifth, and under 2 lengths from the winner. She is peaking at the right time here, and is worth including in all top 4 combos. MCVEIGH (2) ended his 3YO season with an easy maiden win here in April, and looks in good nick at the trials. He has a good draw, and can make a winning return. GILLY'S BOY (1) did what he had to do when winning on debut here 3 weeks ago despite racing greenly. He will be even better with experience, so go again.",
